### Requests for VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio. Start all three APIs first (see README).

@ingest = http://localhost:5100
@receiver = http://localhost:5200
@generator = http://localhost:5300

### Generator: list trades, request types and attachment types
GET {{generator}}/api/samples/options

### Generator: download a sample .eml (omit seed for a random one)
GET {{generator}}/api/samples/email?seed=2026

### Generator: sample .eml with overrides
POST {{generator}}/api/samples/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scenario": { "seed": 99, "requestType": "Renewal", "trade": "Hotel", "claimCount": 2 },
  "attachments": ["submission-pdf"]
}

### Generator: ground-truth facts for a seed (what the AI should extract)
POST {{generator}}/api/samples/scenario
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scenario": { "seed": 99, "requestType": "Renewal", "trade": "Hotel", "claimCount": 2 } }

### End to end: generate -> ingest -> AI receiver
POST {{generator}}/api/samples/email/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scenario": { "trade": "Restaurant / Takeaway" }, "mailbox": "traded" }

### Ingest: preview the AI payload for an .eml on disk (no forwarding)
POST {{ingest}}/api/submissions/preview?mailbox=traded
Content-Type: message/rfc822

< ./data/sample.eml

### Ingest: upload an .eml as multipart and forward it
POST {{ingest}}/api/submissions
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="mailbox"

traded
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.eml"
Content-Type: message/rfc822

< ./data/sample.eml
--boundary--

### Receiver: what has arrived (in-memory, last 100)
GET {{receiver}}/api/ai/submissions
